<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="AnniversarySong-Am-Theme" spTempo="144">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1946
Composer:	Al Jolson and Saul Chaplin
	(official credit; based on Iosif
	 Ivanovici’s “Danube Waves”)
Lyricist:	Al Jolson and Saul Chaplin
Form:	64-bar AABB
Style:	Waltz, can be played as Swing as well.
Key:	E minor

“Anniversary Song,” also known as “Oh, How We
Danced,” was published in 1946 and became closely
associated with Al Jolson’s recording and
performances. Its melody adapts Iosif Ivanovici’s
nineteenth-century waltz “Danube Waves,” so the
official Jolson–Chaplin credit reflects the 
english-language adaptation rather than an entirely
original melody; the 64-bar classification is
customary but may vary by arrangement. </spComments>
